  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-27378529" secondary-reporter="0" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Netherlands Enterprise Agency</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: HortIvoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This four-year project (2020-2024) in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire will train farmers in better and more sustainable practices of producing local vegetables &#x2018;hors sol&#x2019; via the integrated INNOFER model (greenhouse substrate horticulture using Dutch inputs like seeds). This will lead to higher production in amount and quality, which will generate more employment opportunities, better nutrition, food safety, and a bigger market for Dutch enterprises that contribute to the INNOFER model (e.g. via quality inputs).Also, in the shape of a close partnership, the local agroecological institute INFPA will be reinforced in both tacit and non-tacit capacity, since the project will invest in a centre of excellence on their premises in Ti&#xe9;bissou. This centre will provide for training of 240 young farmers and demonstrations for over 3500 farmers from the region.</narrative>
  </description>
